      "writtenOn": "2018-04-04T22:00:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The other option which I initially considered is making this call from without the PD protocol layer in usb_pd_protocol.c. This would be done once VBUS is detected (for SNK) or when VBUS needs to be provided (SRC). But, then after discussing with Aseda, it seemed like this was a cleaner place as this function is already only called when CONFIG_USBC_PPC is defined (and that config would need to be added where it was called in usb_pd_protocol.c. In addition, this is the same place where these lines are being set when they are controlled by the EC. So, I think it might be more confusing to have a call that does something in the case of ANX but then nothing for the case of Parade.",
